We learned to extend them.

A telescope lends distance to the eye. A microphone lends reach to the ear. Language lets one nervous system transmit patterns to another. Science turns doubt into an instrument. Art reveals what measurement misses. And metacognition gives us the strangest trick of all: noticing the lens while we’re looking through it.

We still don’t see everything. But we can compare lenses, test impressions, and sometimes glimpse the shape of what none of us could perceive alone.